

**16.34. Relation of Jacobi's Zeta Function to the Theta Functions**

\[Z(u) = \frac{\partial}{\partial u}\ln\,\Theta(u)\]

\[\begin{array}{l} {16.34.1}\quad\quad Z(u) = \frac{\pi}{2K}\frac{\vartheta_{s}^{\prime}\left(\frac{\pi u}{2K}\right)}{\vartheta_{s}\left(\frac{\pi u}{2K}\right)}\frac{\mbox{cn}\ u\ \mbox{dn}\ u}{\mbox{sn}\ u}\end{array}\]

\[\begin{array}{l} {16.34.2}\quad\quad\quad= \frac{\pi}{2K}\frac{\vartheta_{s}^{\prime}\left(\frac{\pi u}{2K}\right)}{\vartheta_{s}\left(\frac{\pi u}{2K}\right)}\frac{\mbox{dn}\ u\ \mbox{sn}\ u}{\mbox{cn}\ u}\end{array}\]

\[\begin{array}{l} {16.34.3}\quad\quad\quad= \frac{\pi}{2K}\frac{\vartheta_{s}^{\prime}\left(\frac{\pi u}{2K}\right)}{ \vartheta_{s}\left(\frac{\pi u}{2K}\right)}m\,\frac{\mbox{sn}\ u\ \mbox{cn}\ u}{\mbox{dn}\ u}\end{array}\]

\[\begin{array}{l} {16.34.4}\quad\quad= \frac{\pi}{2K}\frac{\vartheta_{s}^{\prime}\left(\frac{\pi u}{2K}\right)}{ \vartheta_{s}\left(\frac{\pi u}{2K}\right)}\end{array}\]

